    "created_at": "2019-04-05T17:43:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-05T17:44:47Z",
    "body": "@Zirro that raises the question then, of how many other CSS properties are we going to turn into meta tags? If in general inline CSS is not usable for some people, should we just make it possible to specify any CSS property of the document via meta tags? I'm not sure this is the right level at which to address peoples' tooling difficulties.\r\n\r\nNote that all CSS loads are render-blocking, so I don't know why color scheme would need to be discovered more-early than other things like background or text color.",
